{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "Strix",
          "informationUri": "https://strix.ai",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CWE-787",
              "name": "sharp 0.32.6 processing untrusted uploads: bundled libvips/libheif/librsvg memory-corruption (CVE-2026-33327 et al.)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "sharp 0.32.6 processing untrusted uploads: bundled libvips/libheif/librsvg memory-corruption (CVE-2026-33327 et al.)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The image-processing library sharp is pinned to 0.32.6, which bundles libvips, libheif and librsvg builds affected by multiple published memory-corruption advisories (GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj, GHSA-rgj7-g3m4-5g8c, GHSA-wq5f-xc86-pv6w). This application processes attacker-supplied images with this exact version on its upload endpoints."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The image-processing library sharp is pinned to 0.32.6, which bundles libvips, libheif and librsvg builds affected by multiple published memory-corruption advisories (GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj, GHSA-rgj7-g3m4-5g8c, GHSA-wq5f-xc86-pv6w). This application processes attacker-supplied images with this exact version on its upload endpoints.\n\nAn authenticated user (any account — registration is open) uploading a crafted image (avatar/photo/exam scan) can trigger memory corruption in the image-decode pipeline. Demonstrated consequence class: process crash (event-loop death → API-wide DoS). Upper bound per advisories: potential RCE on glibc Linux, which would expose the PostgreSQL database holding LGPD-sensitive health data (CPF, exams, mental-health screenings).\n\nUpgrade sharp to >= 0.35.5 (fixes GHSA-wq5f-xc86-pv6w / CVE-2026-96889, which also covers the libvips CVE-2026-33327/33328 and libheif fixes shipped in 0.35.0/0.35.4). Additionally remove `failOn: 'none'` so malformed images are rejected early, and run image decoding in a disposable worker/queue so a crash cannot take the API process down.",
                "markdown": "The image-processing library sharp is pinned to 0.32.6, which bundles libvips, libheif and librsvg builds affected by multiple published memory-corruption advisories (GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj, GHSA-rgj7-g3m4-5g8c, GHSA-wq5f-xc86-pv6w). This application processes attacker-supplied images with this exact version on its upload endpoints.\n\nAn authenticated user (any account — registration is open) uploading a crafted image (avatar/photo/exam scan) can trigger memory corruption in the image-decode pipeline. Demonstrated consequence class: process crash (event-loop death → API-wide DoS). Upper bound per advisories: potential RCE on glibc Linux, which would expose the PostgreSQL database holding LGPD-sensitive health data (CPF, exams, mental-health screenings).\n\nUpgrade sharp to >= 0.35.5 (fixes GHSA-wq5f-xc86-pv6w / CVE-2026-96889, which also covers the libvips CVE-2026-33327/33328 and libheif fixes shipped in 0.35.0/0.35.4). Additionally remove `failOn: 'none'` so malformed images are rejected early, and run image decoding in a disposable worker/queue so a crash cannot take the API process down."
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "7.6",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-787",
                  "CVE-2026-33327",
                  "stride:T",
                  "stride:I"
                ]
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html"
            },
            {
              "id": "CWE-400",
              "name": "nodemailer 9.1.1 quadratic addressparser DoS via attacker-controlled recipients (CVE-2026-90776)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "nodemailer 9.1.1 quadratic addressparser DoS via attacker-controlled recipients (CVE-2026-90776)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "nodemailer is pinned to 9.1.1, which is inside the affected range of a quadratic-complexity address-parsing DoS (CVE-2026-90776 / GHSA-v53p-9fqp-m79j). This application feeds attacker-influenced email addresses into nodemailer on several flows."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "nodemailer is pinned to 9.1.1, which is inside the affected range of a quadratic-complexity address-parsing DoS (CVE-2026-90776 / GHSA-v53p-9fqp-m79j). This application feeds attacker-influenced email addresses into nodemailer on several flows.\n\nAn unauthenticated attacker (lead form, signup) or low-privilege user (reminder/verification mails to their own registered address) can submit a crafted address string that blocks the Node.js event loop for several seconds per request; repeated submissions starve the single-process API and degrade all endpoints for all tenants of this health-data service.\n\nUpgrade nodemailer to >= 10.0.6 (fixes both CVE-2026-90776 and GHSA-v53p-9fqp-m79j). As defense in depth, validate/normalize recipient addresses with a strict RFC 5322 subset before passing them to nodemailer, and cap local-part length.",
                "markdown": "nodemailer is pinned to 9.1.1, which is inside the affected range of a quadratic-complexity address-parsing DoS (CVE-2026-90776 / GHSA-v53p-9fqp-m79j). This application feeds attacker-influenced email addresses into nodemailer on several flows.\n\nAn unauthenticated attacker (lead form, signup) or low-privilege user (reminder/verification mails to their own registered address) can submit a crafted address string that blocks the Node.js event loop for several seconds per request; repeated submissions starve the single-process API and degrade all endpoints for all tenants of this health-data service.\n\nUpgrade nodemailer to >= 10.0.6 (fixes both CVE-2026-90776 and GHSA-v53p-9fqp-m79j). As defense in depth, validate/normalize recipient addresses with a strict RFC 5322 subset before passing them to nodemailer, and cap local-part length."
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-400",
                  "CVE-2026-90776",
                  "stride:D"
                ]
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/400.html"
            },
            {
              "id": "CWE-347",
              "name": "node-forge 1.4.0 (via firebase-admin) RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 signature-forgery vulnerability CVE-2026-85393",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "node-forge 1.4.0 (via firebase-admin) RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 signature-forgery vulnerability CVE-2026-85393"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "node-forge 1.4.0 is present via firebase-admin and fails to validate element count in nested DigestAlgorithm sequences during RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 signature verification (CVE-2026-85393, incomplete fix of CVE-2026-33894). Garbage bytes can be embedded to forge signatures for arbitrary messages under low-exponent RSA keys."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "node-forge 1.4.0 is present via firebase-admin and fails to validate element count in nested DigestAlgorithm sequences during RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 signature verification (CVE-2026-85393, incomplete fix of CVE-2026-33894). Garbage bytes can be embedded to forge signatures for arbitrary messages under low-exponent RSA keys.\n\nIf any reachable code path passed attacker-controlled signed material into node-forge's RSA verification, signatures could be forged. No such path was identified in this codebase; the finding documents the vulnerable dependency for upgrade tracking.\n\nTrack the upstream node-forge fix (incomplete fix of CVE-2026-33894; no fixed release at scan time) and upgrade once published, or override the transitive resolution to a patched build if one ships. No application-side change is required while no signature-verification path reaches node-forge.",
                "markdown": "node-forge 1.4.0 is present via firebase-admin and fails to validate element count in nested DigestAlgorithm sequences during RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 signature verification (CVE-2026-85393, incomplete fix of CVE-2026-33894). Garbage bytes can be embedded to forge signatures for arbitrary messages under low-exponent RSA keys.\n\nIf any reachable code path passed attacker-controlled signed material into node-forge's RSA verification, signatures could be forged. No such path was identified in this codebase; the finding documents the vulnerable dependency for upgrade tracking.\n\nTrack the upstream node-forge fix (incomplete fix of CVE-2026-33894; no fixed release at scan time) and upgrade once published, or override the transitive resolution to a patched build if one ships. No application-side change is required while no signature-verification path reaches node-forge."
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "3.7",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-347",
                  "CVE-2026-85393",
                  "stride:T",
                  "stride:I"
                ]
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/347.html"
            },
