        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-787",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "sharp 0.32.6 processing untrusted uploads: bundled libvips/libheif/librsvg memory-corruption (CVE-2026-33327 et al.)\n\nThe image-processing library sharp is pinned to 0.32.6, which bundles libvips, libheif and librsvg builds affected by multiple published memory-corruption advisories (GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj, GHSA-rgj7-g3m4-5g8c, GHSA-wq5f-xc86-pv6w). This application processes attacker-supplied images with this exact version on its upload endpoints."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "SECURITY.md"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "/workspace/server",
                  "kind": "resource"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "45cac2b0640112da497e617fee8be750253ed6c78b77e40517a3aa1748331051"
          },
          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "7.6",
            "strix_vuln_class_hash": "3cbebc33eef341de2d2b8181fb075316263b3732de6e803f7b649d4be9685401",
            "synthetic_location": true,
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0001",
              "severity": "high",
              "cvss": 7.6,
              "timestamp": "2026-10-08 13:13:03 UTC",
              "target": "/workspace/server",
              "cve": "CVE-2026-33327",
              "cwe": "CWE-787",
              "impact": "An authenticated user (any account — registration is open) uploading a crafted image (avatar/photo/exam scan) can trigger memory corruption in the image-decode pipeline. Demonstrated consequence class: process crash (event-loop death → API-wide DoS). Upper bound per advisories: potential RCE on glibc Linux, which would expose the PostgreSQL database holding LGPD-sensitive health data (CPF, exams, mental-health screenings).",
              "remediation_steps": "Upgrade sharp to >= 0.35.5 (fixes GHSA-wq5f-xc86-pv6w / CVE-2026-96889, which also covers the libvips CVE-2026-33327/33328 and libheif fixes shipped in 0.35.0/0.35.4). Additionally remove `failOn: 'none'` so malformed images are rejected early, and run image decoding in a disposable worker/queue so a crash cannot take the API process down.",
              "dependency_metadata": {
                "package_name": "sharp",
                "installed_version": "0.32.6",
                "advisory_cvss": 7.5,
                "package_ecosystem": "npm",
                "manifest_path": "package.json",
                "fixed_version": "0.35.5",
                "introduced_by": "sharp@0.32.6",
                "dependency_path": "sharp@0.32.6",
                "reachability": "vulnerable_symbol_used",
                "reachability_evidence": "Source-to-sink trace: POST /api/patients/:id/photo (src/routes/patient.routes.ts:321, multer upload.single) → savePatientPhoto (src/utils/storage.ts:108) → optimizeAvatar (src/utils/imageStorage.ts:11) → sharp(buffer, { failOn: 'none' }).resize().jpeg().toBuffer(). Same sink reached by POST /api/doctor/me/photo (src/routes/doctor.routes.ts:444 → src/utils/storage.ts:143), by POST /api/exams file upload (src/routes/exam.routes.ts:151 → saveExamFile → src/utils/storage.ts:159), and by POST /api/medications/scan-photo (aiLimiter-gated but open to any authenticated user). 'failOn: none' at imageStorage.ts:11 explicitly instructs sharp to keep processing malformed images, i.e. the hardened bail-out is disabled on every attacker-reachable path. No image source is trusted-only.",
                "contextual_cvss_breakdown": {
                  "attack_complexity": "L",
                  "attack_vector": "N",
                  "availability": "H",
                  "confidentiality": "L",
                  "integrity": "L",
                  "privileges_required": "L",
                  "scope": "U",
                  "user_interaction": "N"
                },
                "contextual_cvss_score": 7.6,
                "contextual_cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:H",
                "contextual_cvss_reasoning": "sharp 0.32.6 is imported at src/utils/imageStorage.ts:1 and optimizeAvatar() at src/utils/imageStorage.ts:11 calls sharp(buffer, { failOn: 'none' }) on raw upload bytes. The path from the network to this sink is direct: POST /api/patients/:id/photo (src/routes/patient.routes.ts:321, upload.single('photo') → savePatientPhoto → src/utils/storage.ts:108 optimizeAvatar), POST /api/doctor/me/photo (src/routes/doctor.routes.ts:444), exam uploads (POST /api/exams, src/routes/exam.routes.ts:151 upload.single('file')) and POST /api/medications/scan-photo — all require a valid patient/doctor JWT (privileges_required:L), which is freely obtainable via open signup. 'failOn: none' disables sharp's own malformed-input bail-out, widening the accepted input class for libvips/libheif/librsvg image-parsing bugs. In this codebase the demonstrated consequence class is memory corruption in the image pipeline (crash: A:H) with best-case code execution (C:L/I:L scored conservatively; the GHSA upper bounds are higher but require runtime confirmation). Advisory base is CVSSv4 AV:L/PR:L (8.9) because upstream assumed a local file; this deployment feeds it network-sourced authenticated uploads, so attack_vector:N is the honest contextual rating."
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-400",
          "ruleIndex": 1,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "nodemailer 9.1.1 quadratic addressparser DoS via attacker-controlled recipients (CVE-2026-90776)\n\nnodemailer is pinned to 9.1.1, which is inside the affected range of a quadratic-complexity address-parsing DoS (CVE-2026-90776 / GHSA-v53p-9fqp-m79j). This application feeds attacker-influenced email addresses into nodemailer on several flows."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
