                "contextual_cvss_reasoning": "node-forge 1.4.0 is a direct dependency of firebase-admin (node_modules/firebase-admin/package.json dependencies list node-forge), which the app imports for FCM push notifications. I searched src/ for imports of node-forge: none — the app itself never calls node-forge APIs directly, and I found no code path where firebase-admin feeds attacker-supplied certificates or RSA material into node-forge's PKCS#1 v1.5 verification (push-token registration sends only device tokens, not certificates). The vulnerable symbol is therefore present in node_modules but has no demonstrated attacker-controlled call path in this codebase. Per the reachability rubric this is reported as imported with the trace documented and the impact scored conservatively: integrity:L only, high complexity, because exploitation requires a low-exponent RSA key in a path this app does not appear to exercise."
