          "message": {
            "text": "BOLA — object-level authorization on exam lookup (cross-tenant health data) — Requires further review: consulta.ts POST /api/consulta/exams/:examId\n\nconsulta.ts:7 applies router.use(requireAuth) but the only route POST /api/consulta/exams/:examId (lines 10-19) does prisma.exam.findUnique({where:{id: req.params.examId}}) with NO ownerId/userPatientIds scoping — unlike sibling routes. It then renders patient name, age (from dateOfBirth), clinical profile, requesting doctor, and all abnormal exam values into an HTML response. Any authenticated OWNER supplying another user's examId (cuid, non-enumerable but exchanged in shares) gets another patient's health data. Needs dynamic validation by a BOLA validation agent."
