            "text": "Billing webhook spoofing (unauthenticated approval) — Ruled out: POST /api/webhooks/openpix + /api/webhooks/asaas\n\nBoth webhooks verify with the provider before approving: OpenPix (openpix-webhook.routes.ts:81-97) fails closed when OPENPIX_APP_ID missing and rejects unless GET /api/v1/charge/{correlationID} returns status COMPLETED; Asaas (asaas-webhook.routes.ts:97+) fails closed without ASAAS_API_KEY and confirms GET /v3/payments/{id} status RECEIVED*. Both also enforce PENDING status, exact amount match, and correlationID/payment.id existing in DB. A forged payload cannot mint approval without a real provider-side payment. Residual risk (provider outage → all treated as unconfirmed) is fail-closed, not exploitable."
